A||||5||btoth||Spark plug wires... mm?||||5||
Z||000000||btoth||05-28-2001||03:08 PM||||I just noticed that I have 7mm wires on my new V6.  What kind are you using and which are usually better with a stock ignition system?  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||BV MotorSports||05-28-2001||03:13 PM||||I run the 8.8mm Accel wires on my 87GT. Nice wires and I got them from summit racing @  1800 230-3030.<P>steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||05-29-2001||10:47 AM||||I too use the spiral core 8.8 Accels.<BR>These are great wires, I have used them for years on other cars as well.<BR>If you'd like to give them a try the part# is: 110 8879 They usually run from $42-$50.00<BR>Jegs has them too. (800)-345-4545 or <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000003||Alex4mula||05-29-2001||11:11 AM||||I use Jacobs (Jacobs Eletronics). Low low resistance and life time warranty. About $60 direct from them. Lot better than Accel. I did have those too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||05-29-2001||06:17 PM||||What is the best *gauge* of wire to use for the stock ignition?  Is bigger better?  Or only when you have an aftermarket system?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||05-29-2001||09:32 PM||||Whether stock or not, the more voltage you get to your plugs the better. Bigger wires help to protect them from the heat as well as leakage. If you use the Accels you might find that you radio works better too since they don't leak RF noise like the stock ones do. The 8.8 Spiral Core Accels have a life-time warrenty too BTW.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
